# Pinned bootstrap trust anchor for the [omarchy] pacman repo
# (https://pkgs.omarchy.org/stable/$arch — see patches/pacman-stable.conf).
#
# This package is what establishes trust in the omarchy repo's signing key in
# the first place (its post_install scriptlet runs `pacman-key --populate
# omarchy`), so it can't itself be verified by that same key — the standard
# bootstrap problem every *-keyring package has. We pin its exact filename and
# sha256 here, recorded from the repo's own signed database
# (https://pkgs.omarchy.org/stable/x86_64/omarchy.db) at the time this was
# checked, as the trust anchor: build/build.sh fetches this exact file over
# HTTPS and refuses to continue if the hash doesn't match, rather than
# trusting whatever the repo happens to serve at build time.
#
# Bump deliberately (verify the new hash against the repo's own signed .db,
# same way this one was obtained) if omarchy-keyring is ever rotated/updated
# upstream — never silently.

